NexusOS node image configuration
================================

Security bar (same as Phase 2 freeze):
  - API token   (NEXUS_API_TOKEN / --api-token)
  - Join token  (NEXUS_JOIN_TOKEN / --join-token)
  - TLS cert+key (--tls-cert / --tls-key)

Fail-closed model (production / non-smoke image)
------------------------------------------------
- nexusos-coordinator.service is NOT enabled at image build time.
- It has ConditionPathExists on:
    /etc/nexusos/coordinator.env
    /etc/nexusos/tls.crt
    /etc/nexusos/tls.key
- ExecStartPre runs coordinator-preflight.sh (rejects empty / CHANGE_ME* tokens;
  enforces tls.key mode 0600).
- nexusos-firstboot.service (enabled) checks the same; if incomplete it prints
  NEXUSOS_FIRSTBOOT instructions to the serial console / journal and exits 0
  without starting the coordinator. It never invents production secrets.

Provision (recommended)
-----------------------
  nexusos-provision --api-token <TOKEN> --join-token <TOKEN> \
    --advertise https://<this-host>:8080 --start

  # Non-interactive bake / cloud-init style:
  NEXUS_API_TOKEN=... NEXUS_JOIN_TOKEN=... nexusos-provision --yes --start

Manual alternative
------------------
  1. cp /etc/nexusos/coordinator.env.example /etc/nexusos/coordinator.env
  2. Edit tokens and NEXUS_ADVERTISE (must not leave CHANGE_ME*)
  3. Install /etc/nexusos/tls.crt and /etc/nexusos/tls.key (key mode 0600)
  4. systemctl enable --now containerd nexusos-coordinator

Local QEMU smoke (build with --dev-smoke)
-----------------------------------------
  The image is preconfigured with --dev, fixed smoke tokens, and self-signed
  TLS auto-generated by the coordinator. firstboot is disabled; coordinator
  auto-starts. Do not use that mode on real hosts.

See docs/node-image.md in the repository.
